  "method": "CUDA graphs of 2048 dependent torch fill_ kernels on the capture stream; a side-stream node (scalar mul_) is forked from and joined back to the main chain every k main-chain nodes (wait_stream both ways), as SGLang forks kv_a_layernorm once per decoder layer. Each graph is replayed 20 times under torch.profiler; per main-chain kernel the start-to-start interval to the next main-chain kernel is taken, replay boundaries (>20 us) dropped; mean over all replays. The increment is the mean cadence at the published spacing minus the pure-chain mean cadence.",
  "notes": "Every spacing from 16 to 64 except 32 raises the main-chain gap median from 95 to 256 ns; spacings 32 and 128 stay near the chain (972 and 909 ns mean cadence). The published spacing is SGLang v0.5.19 forward_mla.py:329-335 (one kv_a_layernorm fork per MLA layer, about 33 graph nodes per DeepSeek-V3 decode layer); the exception at 32 is a documented sensitivity of this mechanism.",
